{"id":"n5-113","title":"どれでも～","romaji":"dore demo～","jlptLevel":5,"shortExplanation":"Indicates 'any' or 'whichever' when referring to multiple items.","longExplanation":"The どれでも grammar point is used to express that any option or element among multiple choices is acceptable. It can be translated as 'any' or 'whichever' in English. It is often used in questions or suggestions and is commonly seen with でも, but it can also be used with だれでも, いつでも, どこでも, etc.","formation":"どれ + でも","examples":[{"jp":"どれでもいいですか？","romaji":"Dore demo ii desu ka?","en":"Is any choice okay?","words":[{"surface":"どれ","vocabId":null},{"surface":"でも","vocabId":null},{"surface":"いい","vocabId":null,"baseForm":"いう"},{"surface":"です","vocabId":null},{"surface":"か","vocabId":null},{"surface":"？","vocabId":null}],"patternWordIndices":[0,1]},{"jp":"どれでも選んでください。","romaji":"Dore demo erande kudasai.","en":"Please choose whichever you like.","words":[{"surface":"どれ","vocabId":null},{"surface":"でも","vocabId":null},{"surface":"選ん","vocabId":"1588730","reading":"えらぶ","baseForm":"選ぶ"},{"surface":"で","vocabId":null},{"surface":"ください","vocabId":"1184270","reading":"ください","baseForm":"くださる"},{"surface":"。","vocabId":null}],"patternWordIndices":[0,1]},{"jp":"どれでもおいしいです。","romaji":"Dore demo oishii desu.","en":"All of them are delicious.","words":[{"surface":"どれ","vocabId":null},{"surface":"でも","vocabId":null},{"surface":"おいしい","vocabId":"1486650","reading":"おいしい"},{"surface":"です","vocabId":null},{"surface":"。","vocabId":null}],"patternWordIndices":[0,1]},{"jp":"この中でどれでも好きなものを持って行ってください。","romaji":"Kono naka de dore demo suki na mono wo motte itte kudasai.","en":"Please take whichever you like from these.","words":[{"surface":"この","vocabId":null},{"surface":"中","vocabId":"1423310","reading":"なか"},{"surface":"で","vocabId":null},{"surface":"どれ","vocabId":null},{"surface":"でも","vocabId":null},{"surface":"好き","vocabId":"1277450","reading":"すき"},{"surface":"な","vocabId":null,"baseForm":"だ"},{"surface":"もの","vocabId"